        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Foot symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Feet are described as the same as usual, with itch and scale on the soles and between the toes, worse in heat. No pain or spreading redness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Foot examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Moccasin-type fine scale on soles with mild erythema. Interdigital maceration and scale between the 3rd–4th and 4th–5th toes bilaterally; mild malodour. No fissures, increased warmth, cellulitis, or ulcers."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Nail examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Nails are thickened and yellow distally, consistent with onychomycosis; described as unchanged."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Groin symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent groin itch for years, worse with sweating."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Groin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Bilateral erythematous annular plaques with scale in the inguinal folds, consistent with tinea cruris. No obvious secondary bacterial infection."
      }
    },
    {
